A||N||10||Haze_Performance||Gauge upgrade question||||5||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||08-19-2000||01:11 AM||||Well Im bidding on a complete GT cluster on Ebay (No radio pod gauges) I would like to swap out my complete 85mph cluster out of my 85 Coupe. I know Ill lose the oil press. gauge, but thats ok. What do I have to do to complete the swap?? What must I do to get the GT style Speedo, Tach, Fuel and Temp to work in my car??<P>Thank You<BR>Carl <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg"> My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe<P><BR>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-19-2000||01:29 AM||||Pay close attention 'cause this is a toughy.  <P>1)  Unplug the old gauge cluster (3 connectors).<P>2)  Unbolt same from dash and remove.<P>3)  Bolt in new gauge cluster.<P>4)  Plug <B>all 3</B> connectors back in.<P>5)  Drive car.<P>It's basically just that simple.  You do have to remove the switches, rear and lower trim pieces, then remove the main part.  You'll see what I mean when you do it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||08-19-2000||11:17 AM||||I heard that the GT (V6) Tach might read diffrent then my NON-GT (L4) Tach? Is that true?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg"> My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe<P><BR>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||5
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||08-20-2000||06:35 AM||||Anyone??<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg"> My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe<P><BR>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||5
Z||000004||Will||08-20-2000||09:20 AM||||Yes, the Tach will read differently.<P>Try this site:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/Tach.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/Tach.html</A> <P>It has info on recalibrating a tach.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BBBAD GT||08-20-2000||10:41 AM||||Haze:<P>Here is a different approach, which I'm probably going to do.  Automter has 3 3/8" tach and speedo that fit perfect in the holes from the former gauges (look at batboy's project).  The sport-comp units look pretty good.  I'm also going to get some electrical 2 1/16" or 2 5/8" sport comp gauges to put in the pod above the radio/heating consol.  I priced them at carparts.com, and it came to approx $200 for the whole set (tach/speedo/oil pres/water temp/amps) cluster with their famous 33% off sale.  Now, I'm not sure how easy it is to hook up the speedo or the tach, but it can be done since batboy did it.  Yell at me if you want more information/pricing on differnt brands, the Z series wasn't too much more.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||08-20-2000||11:02 AM||||Remember that BB is running a carbed V8.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BBBAD GT||08-20-2000||01:16 PM||||So am I  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But seriously, the speedo would be the most difficult task of all of the gauge install.  The oil press/water temp/volt isn't tough at all, they make adaptors for just about anything.  At worst, you might have to use the stock sender hole in the motor, but you are gaining much more accurate reading of the gauges, I found that out with my 5.0<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||ur2biteme||08-21-2000||04:05 AM||||when i changed over my 87 4cyl gagues to an 85 gt's, i just swapped the boards on the back.  i don't think they are exact (i think that 5200r.p.m. on the gague is actually aprox. 5000 r.p.m., due to the gt gagues going to 6500 and the originals reading 6000 on the same sweep), but they're darn close like that.  <P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>165k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
Z||000009||Indiana_resto_guy||08-21-2000||01:04 PM||||carl,<P>I sent you an E-Mail. 362K, will take a while to down load. Should take care of you.||||reg||1
